[2026-10-24T14:59:09.022Z] [INFO]     "stdout": "title:\tAdd a share option for all links variants\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tkonard (Konstantin Diachenko)\nlabels:\tdocumentation, enhancement\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t17\n--\nOnce we click to share links network variant, we should go to final editor, where we can change how it is rendered as SVG and download PNG and other formats so on as needed.\n\nThe share small icon should be shown only when links network card is hovered with mouse, or we click the card itself and that goes to the page of card which is mostly done for visuals configuration of specific links network image and sharing into social media.\n\nAt this page we should be able also to see math notation as per theory, numeric representation as N-ary number, and links notation representation, all of which should be editable, so we have ability to draw exactly any links network configuration and share it, but we start from one we clicked on.\n\nSo that is separate page dedicated to links network viewing, editing and sharing.\n\nWe should have as much configurations as possible.\n\nFor example for the links shape itself we should be able to configure angle at which link comes to another link.\n\nThe start of link shape, the end of link shape and so on.\n\nSo each and detail perfectly configurable.\n\nAlso colors and so on.\n\nThe background, if it is transparent, borders of card, style of them and so on.\n\nDo we need card at all or just use plain black background and links shapes.\n\nWe also need to add experimental option to solve for lines collisions, so we draw link entering or comming away at specific angle, so we reduce overlapping between links shapes.\n\n\n\n\n[]title:\t[WIP] Add a share option for all links variants\nstate:\tDRAFT\nauthor:\tkonard (Konstantin Diachenko)\nlabels:\t\nassignees:\tkonard (Konstantin Diachenko)\nreviewers:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nnumber:\t18\nurl:\thttps://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/18\nadditions:\t1\ndeletions:\t0\nauto-merge:\tdisabled\n--\n## 🤖 AI-Powered Solution Draft\n\nThis pull request is being automatically generated to solve issue #17.\n\n### 📋 Issue Reference\nFixes #17\n\n### 🚧 Status\n**Work in Progress** - The AI assistant is currently analyzing and implementing the solution draft.\n\n### 📝 Implementation Details\n_Details will be added as the solution draft is developed..._\n\n---\n*This PR was created automatically by the AI issue solver*\n[]total 288\ndrwxr-xr-x 20 box  box    4096 Oct 24 14:58 .\ndrwxrwxrwt  1 root root   4096 Oct 24 14:58 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x  8 box  box    4096 Oct 24 14:58 .git\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 box  box    4096 Oct 24 14:58 .github\n-rw-r--r--  1 box  box     433 Oct 24 14:58 .gitignore\n-rw-r--r--  1 box  box     169 Oct 24 14:58 .gitkeep\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 box  box    4096 Oct 24 14:58 .husky\n-rw-r--r--  1 box  box     163 Oct 24 14:58 .prettierignore\n-rw-r--r--  1 box  box      47 Oct 24 14:58 .prettierrc\n-rw-r--r--  1 box  box      92 Oct 24 14:58 .secretlintrc.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 box  box    4313 Oct 24 14:58 README.md\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 box  box    4096 Oct 24 14:58 art\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 box  box    4096 Oct 24 14:58 associative\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 box  box    4096 Oct 24 14:58 blog\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 box  box    4096 Oct 24 14:58 ci-logs\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 box  box    4096 Oct 24 14:58 cv\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 box  box    4096 Oct 24 14:58 dev\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 box  box    4096 Oct 24 14:58 docs\n-rw-r--r--  1 box  box    1271 Oct 24 14:58 eslint.config.js\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 box  box    4096 Oct 24 14:58 experience\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 box  box    4096 Oct 24 14:58 experiments\n-rw-r--r--  1 box  box    1935 Oct 24 14:58 index.html\n-rw-r--r--  1 box  box  161309 Oct 24 14:58 package-lock.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 box  box    1978 Oct 24 14:58 package.json\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 box  box    4096 Oct 24 14:58 public\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 box  box    4096 Oct 24 14:58 repositories\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 box  box    4096 Oct 24 14:58 research\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 box  box    4096 Oct 24 14:58 scripts\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 box  box    4096 Oct 24 14:58 settings\ndrwxr-xr-x 11 box  box    4096 Oct 24 14:58 src\n-rw-r--r--  1 box  box    2429 Oct 24 14:58 vite.config.js\nb400fb6 Initial commit with task details\n1479043 Merge pull request #16 from konard/issue-15-c7170c04f74e\naa1f10b Remove the .gitkeep of the initial commit (issue #15)\n5a19312 Dependencies: fast-uri 3.1.8 → its fixed release (npm audit fix), four moderate advisories of a dependency of secretlint failed the audit of CI (issue #15)\n4a632bc Case study of issue #15: every requirement with where it is done and what verifies it, the root causes (the Skin jump of CSS multi-column with logs of three browsers, saturate(100) of the glass, the click of mica, the clipped top bar of phones), the background layers, frames, sound and presets, mobile measurements of main and this branch, the check of every screen, a comparison with konard/immortality, libraries and research, limits (issue #15)\n65ae935 Responsive: on phones the pages get a row of their own in the top bar and the current page is scrolled into view (main showed one and a half links, and on 768 px the current page could be hidden), the section links stay on phones (only the ↑ was left), a row of links fades out only at an edge with more links behind it, the checkbox of the blog filter is no longer stretched; a check of 9 pages × 4 widths × 2 themes (main fails 7, this branch none) with screenshots (issue #15)\nf87eaba Performance on phones: the code shared by all pages no longer carries the career data (Layout 111.5 → 90.8 kB gzip), the home page links to the CVs without the CV builder, and a governor lowers the resolution and then the frame rate of the universe, and the frame rate of stars and beams, while the page cannot keep up; a mobile measurement script (4× slower CPU, slow 4G) with results for main and this branch (issue #15)\nad3f6a2 Presets: 9 looks of the site with miniatures drawn from their settings (Default, Calm, Matrix, Deep space, Warp, Neon HUD, Liquid, Blueprint, Light and fast), looks saved in this browser (save, apply, update, rename, delete, copy as JSON and load in another browser, synced between tabs), a random look never heavier than the defaults, a #settings= link that carries the look and keeps the one it replaced; a look never changes the motion, volume or notation; preset code loaded only on the settings page or with such a link (issue #15)\n70139ab Sound design: 31 synthesized sounds (26 from konard/immortality, the Unlicense, and 5 new), up to four sounds per interaction played at random, in turn or together, a level for each, volume, tone, room echo and size, pitch variation, stereo towards the pointer, a ▶ for every sound and a switch in the top bar; the sound code is loaded only when sound is on; a gain silent before its first event (one sample of full-scale noise made mica 15 times louder); settings shared by all tabs come before the tabs (issue #15)\nf41eff4 Futuristic frames: each corner on its own (7 shapes, 5 lines, size), tiles with previews of every corner, a stylesheet generated from the shapes and its test (issue #15)\n3c307e3 Background: up to four star layers (12 shapes, size, colours, glow, twinkling, spin, drift, warp and orbit, trails, blending), beams along the grid lines, grid styles (lines, dashes, crosses, dots) and colours, colours, zoom and star size of the universe; star and beam code is loaded only when switched on; a test that every setting is used by a stylesheet or a script (issue #15)\n68b9397 Glass skin: one rule gives every panel the blur and the corner radius (page cards, Habr cards, the language cloud, theory panels had no blur before), new options: colour behind panels, borders and lines, shadow, light on the upper edge; test that percents above 2 are divided by 100 (saturate(100) painted the panels blue) (issue #15)\n7865728 Settings page: sections in two fixed columns instead of CSS multi-column (Skin no longer jumps between columns, equal column tops in Safari), every row a label | control | value | reset grid; schema split into fields, background and skins files (issue #15)\n1f0b1d2 New defaults from issue #15 (universe, grid, rain and glass), a setting for the space around every rain symbol, rain glow scaled to device pixels (it was half as large on Retina screens), the issue data and screenshots (issue #15)\n07ec4e9 Initial commit with task details\n4c06074 Merge pull request #14 from konard/issue-13-b89681e2026e\n70c312d Case study of issue #13: the rain root cause (WebKit runs module scripts before the CSS, canvases stretched ×4.27), settings, skins, real references, the stack and the notation, with screenshots; .gitkeep removed (issue #13)\n4b441c4 Associative stack from link-foundation/meta-theory up to the applications: 13 layers with every original repository of linksplatform, link-foundation and link-assistant in exactly one of them (191 in all), a layer index; link-foundation/lfs collected (issue #13)\naa11c92 Links theory notation: L → L² (draft 0.0.2, default) or R → R² (draft 0.0.3) from the settings, in the theory formulas (Tₙ = Rⁿ, L = R × Tₙ, N²: R → R × R), the motto, the stack and the positions (issue #13)\n936a6e5 Skins: liquid glass (blur, saturation, tint, light on the edges, depth, sheen, floating capsules, refraction in Chromium) and futuristic HUD after konard/immortality (12 palettes, 8 frames, 9 surfaces, glow, fonts, titles, hover, scanlines); the glass skin's opacity, blur and radius are settings too (issue #13)",
