[2026-10-24T14:59:13.229Z] [INFO]     "role": "user",
[2026-10-24T14:59:13.229Z] [INFO]     "content": [
[2026-10-24T14:59:13.229Z] [INFO]       {
[2026-10-24T14:59:13.229Z] [INFO]         "tool_use_id": "toolu_01AbuJ4MdGN63mLDNXnhhnKc",
[2026-10-24T14:59:13.229Z] [INFO]         "type": "tool_result",
[2026-10-24T14:59:13.229Z] [INFO]         "content": "# konard.github.io\n\nPersonal website of Konstantin Diachenko ([@konard](https://github.com/konard)): a public biography and CV with infographics.\nIt is published at https://konard.github.io.\n\nThe site is in English and Russian, and has light and dark themes.\n\n- The language comes from `?lang=en|ru`, then the remembered choice, then the browser.\n- The theme follows the system until it is switched in the top bar.\n\n`/cv/?role=<position>&style=<classic|compact|technical|academic>&lang=<en|ru>` shows a CV for one of 15 positions, or the full record without `role`.\nIts \"Download PDF\" button links to the PDF printed at deploy time, `/cv/pdf/konstantin-diachenko-<position>-<style>-<lang>.pdf`.\n\nIt is a React 19 app built with [Vite](https://vite.dev) and tested with [Vitest](https://vitest.dev), with hand-written SVG/CSS charts and no runtime API calls.\nAll numbers come from data snapshots committed to the repository.\n\n## Development\n\n```bash\nnpm ci\nnpm start          # dev server at http://localhost:3000\nnpm run test:ci    # unit, data and workflow tests\nnpm run check      # ESLint, Prettier, file size limits and secret scan\nnpm run build      # production build in build/\nnpm run build:cv   # prints every CV of build/ to build/cv/pdf/ (needs `npx playwright install chromium`)\n```\n\n`npm run build:cv` fails if:\n\n- a CV for a position takes more than 2 pages;\n- a compact CV takes more than 1 page;\n- a PDF has no text layer;\n- a part of the CV is positioned, which would put its text out of reading order for ATS parsers.\n\n`npm run build:cv -- --verbose rust` prints only the Rust CVs and lists their page counts.\n\n## Updating the data\n\n| What                                                          | Where                                |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| Jobs (EN/RU texts, dates, bullets for the CV, tags and roles) | `src/data/experience.js`             |\n| Positions: their jobs, skills, products and CV strengths      | `src/data/positions.js`              |\n| Education, skills, publications, contacts, featured projects  | `src/data/profile.js` (hand-curated) |\n| GitHub, npm, crates.io, NuGet and Stack Overflow numbers      | `src/data/github.json` (generated)   |\n\nTo refresh the generated data:\n\n```bash\nexperiments/collect-github-data.sh       # repositories and organizations (needs gh auth)\nexperiments/collect-contributions.sh     # yearly contribution totals (GraphQL)\nnpm run build:data                       # writes src/data/github.json\n```\n\n`src/data/data.test.js` fails if `github.json` is out of date with the snapshots.\n\n## Deployment\n\n`.github/workflows/github-pages.yml` lints the workflows (actionlint), runs `npm run check` and `npm audit`, then the tests and the build, for pull requests and for pushes to `main`.\nThe `test` job prints the CV PDFs into the build with `npm run build:cv`, then uploads the tested build as the GitHub Pages artifact.\nOn `main`, the `deploy` job publishes that artifact with `actions/deploy-pages`, then `scripts/check-deployed-site.sh` fails the run unless https://konard.github.io serves the app.\n\nGitHub Pages must be set to **Settings → Pages → Build and deployment → Source: GitHub Actions**.\nNothing is committed to `docs/`; it only holds the case studies.\n\n## Case studies\n\n- [`issue-1`](docs/case-studies/issue-1/README.md): the research, requirements, alternatives and decisions behind the site.\n- [`issue-7`](docs/case-studies/issue-7/README.md): repositories by field, roles, research and link visuals.\n- [`issue-9`](docs/case-studies/issue-9/README.md): link networks, the problem solving diagram and the ecosystem.\n- [`issue-11`](docs/case-studies/issue-11/README.md): the experience synced with hh.ru, a CV per position in EN/RU, the PDF styles and the themes.\n- [`issue-13`](docs/case-studies/issue-13/README.md): the rain on Safari, the settings page, the liquid glass and futuristic skins, only real references, the full associative stack and the R → R² notation.\n- [`issue-15`](docs/case-studies/issue-15/README.md): the new defaults and a test that every setting is applied, the settings layout, the sound design, background layers, each corner of the futuristic frames, presets and saved looks, phones and every screen.\n{\n  \"name\": \"konard.github.io\",\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@fontsource/chakra-petch\": \"^5.3.0\",\n    \"@fontsource/electrolize\": \"^5.3.0\",\n    \"@fontsource/orbitron\": \"^5.3.0\",\n    \"@fontsource/share-tech-mono\": \"^5.3.0\",\n    \"react\": \"^19.0.0\",\n    \"react-dom\": \"^19.0.0\"\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"start\": \"vite\",\n    \"build\": \"vite build\",\n    \"preview\": \"vite preview\",\n    \"test\": \"vitest\",\n    \"test:ci\": \"vitest run\",\n    \"lint\": \"eslint . --max-warnings=0\",\n    \"format\": \"prettier --write .\",\n    \"format:check\": \"prettier --check .\",\n    \"check:file-size\": \"bash scripts/check-file-line-limits.sh\",\n    \"check\": \"npm run lint && npm run format:check && npm run check:file-size && npm run check:secrets\",\n    \"build:data\": \"node scripts/build-data.cjs\",\n    \"build:frames\": \"node scripts/build-frames-css.mjs\",\n    \"check:secrets\": \"[REDACTED]\\\"**/*\\\" --secretlintignore .pr…re\",\n    \"prepare\": \"husky\",\n    \"build:cv\": \"node scripts/build-cv-pdf.mjs\"\n  },\n  \"homepage\": \"https://konard.github.io\",\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@eslint/js\": \"^10.0.1\",\n    \"@secretlint/secretlint-rule-preset-recommend\": \"^13.0.7\",\n    \"@testing-library/dom\": \"^10.4.2\",\n    \"@testing-library/jest-dom\": \"^6.9.1\",\n    \"@testing-library/react\": \"^16.3.3\",\n    \"@vitejs/plugin-react\": \"^6.1.2\",\n    \"eslint\": \"^10.13.0\",\n    \"eslint-plugin-react-hooks\": \"^7.1.1\",\n    \"eslint-plugin-react-refresh\": \"^0.5.7\",\n    \"globals\": \"^17.13.0\",\n    \"husky\": \"^9.1.7\",\n    \"js-yaml\": \"^4.3.2\",\n    \"jsdom\": \"^30.1.3\",\n    \"lint-staged\": \"^17.6.0\",\n    \"playwright\": \"^1.64.1\",\n    \"prettier\": \"^3.9.10\",\n    \"secretlint\": \"^13.0.7\",\n    \"vite\": \"^8.3.4\",\n    \"vitest\": \"^5.0.5\"\n  },\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"engines\": {\n    \"node\": \">=22\"\n  },\n  \"lint-staged\": {\n    \"*.{js,jsx,cjs,mjs}\": [\n      \"eslint --fix --max-warnings=0 --no-warn-ignored\",\n      \"prettier --write\"\n    ],\n    \"*.{css,md,html,json,yml,yaml}\": [\n      \"prettier --write\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\nimport { resolve } from 'node:path';\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite';\nimport react from '@vitejs/plugin-react';\nimport { applySettings, normalize } from './src/settings/apply.js';\nimport { CSS_RULES } from './src/settings/schema.js';\n\n// Every page is its own HTML entry (a real URL on GitHub Pages, no client-side\n// routing). The home page must stay `index` so build/index.html keeps its name.\nconst PAGES = ['repositories', 'experience', 'research', 'associative', 'art', 'blog', 'cv', 'settings'];\nconst input = Object.fromEntries([\n  ['index', resolve(import.meta.dirname, 'index.html')],\n  ...PAGES.map((page) => [page, resolve(import.meta.dirname, page, 'index.html')]),\n]);\n\n// Applies the light or dark theme before the first paint, so a light-theme\n// visitor never sees a dark flash. The rules match src/i18n/prefs.js: the\n// remembered choice, otherwise prefers-color-scheme.\nexport const THEME_SCRIPT = `(function(){try{var t=localStorage.getItem('theme');if(t!=='light'&&t!=='dark'){t=matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: light)').matches?'light':'dark'}document.documentElement.dataset.theme=t}catch(e){document.documentElement.dataset.theme='dark'}})();`;\n\n// Applies the remembered settings (skin, background, notation; issue #13)\n// before the first paint with the same rules as src/settings/store.js, so a\n// visitor with the futuristic skin never sees the glass one first.\nconst inline = (fn) => String(fn).replace(/\\s*\\n\\s*/g, ' ');\nexport const SETTINGS_SCRIPT = `(function(){try{${inline(normalize)};${inline(applySettings)};var r=${JSON.stringify(CSS_RULES)};applySettings(document.documentElement,r,normalize(r,JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('settings')||'{}')))}catch(e){}})();`;\n\nconst themeBeforePaint = () => ({\n  name: 'theme-before-paint',\n  transformIndexHtml: () => [{ tag: 'script', children: THEME_SCRIPT + SETTINGS_SCRIPT, injectTo: 'head-prepend' }],\n});\n\n// The site is served from the root of https://konard.github.io, and the\n// deploy job publishes build/ with actions/deploy-pages (see .github/workflows/github-pages.yml).\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [react(), themeBeforePaint()],\n  build: {\n    outDir: 'build',\n    sourcemap: true,\n    rollupOptions: { input },\n  },\n  server: {\n    port: 3000,\n  },\n  test: {\n    environment: 'jsdom',\n    globals: true,\n    setupFiles: './src/setupTests.js',\n    include: ['src/**/*.test.{js,jsx}'],\n    testTimeout: 10000,\n  },\n});\nsrc/setupTests.js\nsrc/workflow.test.js\nsrc/App.test.jsx\nsrc/skins.future.css\nsrc/skins.liquid.css\nsrc/App.css\nsrc/App.jsx\nsrc/skins.frames.test.jsx\nsrc/App.media.css\nsrc/index.css\nsrc/skins.palettes.css\nsrc/skins.frames.css\nsrc/skins.frames.js\nsrc/skins.test.jsx\nsrc/skins.glass.css\nsrc/Layout.css\nsrc/index.jsx\nsrc/App.sections.css\nsrc/components/Sound.jsx\nsrc/components/LanguagesChart.jsx\nsrc/components/RepoList.jsx\nsrc/components/Skills.jsx\nsrc/components/HabrCards.jsx\nsrc/components/Projects.jsx\nsrc/components/ProblemSolvingDiagram.jsx\nsrc/components/ContributionsChart.jsx\nsrc/components/Contacts.jsx\nsrc/components/visuals.test.jsx\nsrc/components/ProblemSolving.jsx\nsrc/components/Registries.jsx\nsrc/components/PageCards.jsx\nsrc/components/LanguageCloud.jsx\nsrc/components/edges.js\nsrc/components/Timelin