[2026-10-24T15:08:18.043Z] [INFO]         "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Write</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Solve GitHub issue https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/issues/17, \"Add a share option for all links variants\" (labels: documentation, enhancement; it has no comments). Work in /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1792853904677 on branch `issue-17-c029b2b48293`. Update the existing draft PR #18 (https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/18), whose body currently says \"Fixes #17\", and keep that closing keyword. Push only to this branch. Do not stop until every requirement is implemented and verified. When finished: run local checks, make CI pass, run `gh pr ready 18`, and update the PR title and description with gh pr edit.\n\n   The issue text, in summary:\n   - Clicking \"share\" on a links-network card goes to a final editor page. There the user can change how the network is rendered as SVG and download PNG and other formats.\n   - A small share icon appears only when the card is hovered with the mouse. Clicking the card itself also goes to the card's page, which is mostly for configuring the visuals of that network image and sharing it to social media.\n   - The page shows three representations of the network, all editable: math notation per the theory, a numeric representation as an N-ary number, and links notation. With these the user can draw exactly any links network configuration, starting from the one that was clicked.\n   - It is a separate page dedicated to viewing, editing and sharing a links network.\n   - It should have as many configuration options as possible. Examples from the issue: the angle at which a link comes to another link, the shape of the link start and end, \"each and every detail perfectly configurable\", colours, background (including transparent), card borders and their style. The issue also asks whether a card is needed at all, or just a plain black background with the link shapes.\n   - An experimental option to solve line collisions: a link enters or leaves at a specific angle so that link shapes overlap less.\n\n   Guidelines from the system prompt:\n   - Commit atomic steps, write reproducing tests, and keep experiments in ./experiments.\n   - For visual work, save screenshots in the repo and link them in the PR as `https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-17-c029b2b48293/<path>?raw=true`.\n   - Follow the repo style. Merged PRs add a case study `docs/case-studies/issue-N/README.md` and a README \"Case studies\" entry, and commit messages are long and descriptive, ending with \"(issue #N)\".\n   - Run `npm run check` (ESLint, Prettier, file-size limit of 1500 lines, secretlint) and `npm run test:ci` before pushing.\n   - Remove the `.gitkeep` from the initial commit; the previous PR did this.\n   - Check that main is merged into the branch, and check comments on the issue and the PR before finishing.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - React 19 + Vite multi-page app. Each page is an HTML entry listed in the `PAGES` array in vite.config.js (`['repositories','experience','research','associative','art','blog','cv','settings']`). Each page has `<page>/index.html` with meta/og tags, a `src/pages/<page>.jsx` that calls `mount(Page)`, and a component that uses `Layout`.\n   - Vitest with jsdom, setupFiles `./src/setupTests.js`, tests at `src/**/*.test.{js,jsx}`. `@testing-library/react` is available, and so is the playwright devDependency.\n   - Bilingual texts are `{en, ru}` objects translated with `useLang().t`. Plurals use `plural(k, lang, forms)` from src/i18n/plural.\n   - Theory notation setting `theory.notation` is 'L' or 'R'. `useNotation()` comes from src/links/notation.js. Doublet formula: L is `λ: L → L × L`, R is `N²: R → R × R`.\n   - Network code \"01 20\": link i+1 is [source, target], the references are 0..n, and the code is 2n digits in base n+1. configurations.js provides decode, encode, codeAt, indexOf, mathNotation (\"01₃ 20₃\"), linksNotation, networkCount, representatives, classCount, canonical.\n   - Settings field helpers in src/settings/fields.js: `range(key,d,min,max,step,label,extra)`, `toggle`, `select`, `color`, `option(value,en,ru)`. Settings page CSS classes: `setting`, `settings__fields`, `setting__input`, `setting__value`, `setting__reset`, `settings__group`, `settings__head`.\n   - CSS variables: dark `--link-1..4` are #22d3ee, #c084fc, #f472b6, #facc15; light are #0e7490, #9333ea, #db2777, #b45309. Also `--bg:#070b14`, `--surface:#0d1220`, `--border`, `--accent`.\n   - CI: .github/workflows/github-pages.yml runs actionlint, then `npm run check` and `npm audit --audit-level=moderate`, then `test:ci`, build, and `build:cv` with Playwright Chromium.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **src/links/glyph.js** (modified). Default output was verified byte-identical for all 21,081 gallery networks (n=1..3 all, n=4 representatives) against the snapshot `/tmp/baseline/glyphs.json`.\n     - New exports:\n       - `MAX_LINKS = 9`.\n       - `COLORS` extended to 9 colours: `['#22d3ee','#c084fc','#f472b6','#facc15','#34d399','#fb923c','#60a5fa','#f87171','#a3e635']`.\n       - `MARKERS = ['bar','arrow','triangle','tail','dot','circle','square','diamond','none']`.\n       - `SHAPE` defaults: `{rotation:0, spread:1, padding:9, tension:0.38, bulge:20, gap:0.07, free:1, loop:1, lens:true, angles:'mirror', sourceAngle:30, targetAngle:30, start:'bar', startSize:3.6, startAngle:28, end:'arrow', endSize:5.5, endAngle:28, middle:'none', middleSize:2.2, turns:[]}`.\n       - `shapeOf(shape)`.\n       - `layout(n, {rotation, spread})`. The start angle is π for n=2, -3π/4 for n=4, and -π/2 otherwise.\n       - `layoutCurves(links, shape)` returns curves in layout units for the collision solver. It throws RangeError outside 1..MAX_LINKS.\n       - `glyphCurves(links, shape)` returns curves scaled into SIZE=100. Each curve now also has `middle: {at, dir}`.\n       - `marker(kind, at, dir, size, angle)` returns `{d, fill}`.\n       - `glyphParts(links, shape)` returns `{line, start, end, middle, color}` per link.\n       - `glyphPaths(links, shape)` returns `{d: line+start.d+end.d+middle.d, color}`.\n       - `glyphSvg` is unchanged.\n     - Internals:\n       - `approach(d, chord, twice, angle, o)`: mirror mode is `lens(reflect(d, chord), chord, twice && o.lens)`; fixed mode is `rotate(chord, side*angle)`, where side follows the mirror's cross sign.\n       - `linkCurve(links, i, places, o)` applies per-link turns `o.turns[i] = [sourceDeg, targetDeg]` to free ends, loops (`away`) and reference ends.\n   - **src/settings/fields.js** (modified): appended `decimals` and the exported `formatValue(field, value)`, moved from SettingsPage.\n   - **src/pages/SettingsPage.jsx** (modified): removed the local `decimals` and `formatValue`, added `import { formatValue } from '../settings/fields';` and `export { formatValue };`. settings.test.jsx still imports it from './SettingsPage'.\n   - **src/links/edit.js** (new). Exports:\n     - `check(links)` returns `{links}` or `{error:{en,ru}}` (1..9 links, references 0..n).\n     - `parseCode(text)` accepts \"0120\", \"01 20\", \"01-20\" or \"01.20\" and returns \"01 20\" or null.\n     - `parseNumber(text)` reads \"0120₃\" or \"0120_3\". The suffix is matched with `/(?:([₀-₉]+)|_(\\d+))$/`, and the base must equal n+1.\n     - `countOf(n)` is a BigInt.\n     - `parseIndex(text, n)` uses BigInt.\n     - `parseLinks(text)` reads \"(1: 0 1) (2: 2 0)\", with or without names, via `byNames`.\n     - `parseMath(text)` reads \"λ = {1 ↦ (0, 1), 2 ↦ (2, 0)}\" (also `->`, `→`, `=>`, `:`), or the subscripted pairs \"01₃ 20₃\".\n     - `functionOf(notation)` gives λ or N². `signatureOf(notation)`.\n     - `theoryNotation(links, notation)`, `numberNotation(links)` (