[2026-10-24T15:16:42.269Z] [INFO]         "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Write</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Solve GitHub issue https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/issues/17, \"Add a share option for all links variants\". The issue has no comments. Work in /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1792853904677 on branch `issue-17-c029b2b48293`. Update the existing draft PR #18 (https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/18) and keep \"Fixes #17\" in its body. Push only to this branch. Do not stop until every requirement is implemented and verified.\n\n   **What the issue asks for:**\n   - A share icon on each links-network card, shown only on mouse hover. It leads to a separate editor/share page.\n   - Clicking the card itself also opens that page.\n   - On the page:\n     - three editable representations of the network: math notation per the theory, an N-ary number, and links notation. With them the user can draw any configuration, starting from the one that was clicked;\n     - as many configuration options as possible: angles at which links meet, the shapes of the start and end, colours, background (including transparent), card borders and their style;\n     - a choice between a card and a plain black background;\n     - downloads of PNG and other formats, and sharing to social media;\n     - an experimental option that reduces line collisions by changing the angles at which links enter and leave.\n\n   **When finished:**\n   - run `npm run check` and `npm run test:ci`, and make CI pass;\n   - add a case study at docs/case-studies/issue-17/README.md, a README \"Case studies\" entry, and screenshots linked with `https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-17-c029b2b48293/<path>?raw=true`;\n   - remove `.gitkeep`;\n   - write commit messages that are long and descriptive and end with \"(issue #17)\";\n   - merge main if needed and check the comments on the issue and the PR;\n   - update the PR title and description with `gh pr edit`, then run `gh pr ready 18`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **App structure:** React 19 + Vite multi-page app. Each page needs a `PAGES` entry in vite.config.js, a `<page>/index.html`, a `src/pages/<page>.jsx` that calls `mount(Page)`, and a `Layout page=... sections=[[id,label]]` wrapper.\n   - **Tests:** Vitest with jsdom and @testing-library/react. Experiments are run with `npx vite-node experiments/x.mjs`, because plain node fails on the extensionless imports.\n   - **Formatting:** Prettier with singleQuote and printWidth 120. ESLint uses react-hooks v7, so avoid setState in effects and reading refs during render.\n   - **i18n:** `useLang().t({en,ru})` and `plural(count, lang, {en:[..],ru:[..]})`. Russian needs the genitive after «из». `formatNumber(v, lang)` lives in src/components/format.js.\n   - **Notation:** `useNotation().notation` is 'L' or 'R'.\n   - **Network codes:** \"01 20\", where link i+1 is [source, target] with references 0..n, in base n+1. `canonical(links)` returns a code string, so decode it.\n   - **Light-theme colours:** CSS `svg [data-link='1..4']` overrides glyph colours in the light theme. The editor preview injects an SVG string without data-link, so its colours stay exact.\n   - **Gallery tests** (src/pages/pages.test.jsx) must keep passing:\n     - li textContent equals the math notation only ('00₂');\n     - li title equals the links notation;\n     - 162 `path` elements for n=2, so a share icon must use circle/line elements, not path;\n     - the list aria-label is \"Networks of 2 links\".\n   - **Settings CSS classes** reused by the editor: `settings__group`, `settings__head`, `settings__lead`, `settings__fields`, `setting setting--<type> is-changed`, `setting__input`, `setting__value`, `setting__reset`, `setting__hint`, `button button--small`. They come from src/pages/settings.css, which the network page must import.\n   - **No `.visually-hidden` class exists**, so network.css must add it.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   **Done before the earlier summary:**\n   - **src/links/glyph.js** (modified, 322 lines):\n     - exports `SIZE=100`, `STROKE=2.4`, `MAX_LINKS=9`, `COLORS` (9), `MARKERS`, `SHAPE`;\n     - `layout`, `bezier`, `shapeOf`, `layoutCurves` (throws RangeError outside 1..9), `glyphCurves`;\n     - `marker(kind, at, dir, size, angle)` returns `{d, fill}`;\n     - `glyphParts(links, shape)` returns `[{line,start,end,middle,color}]`;\n     - `glyphPaths`, `glyphSvg`.\n     - Per-link `turns[i] = [sourceDeg, targetDeg]`. The output for the default shape is byte-identical to the baseline.\n   - **src/settings/fields.js**: `formatValue` moved here. **src/pages/SettingsPage.jsx** imports it and re-exports it.\n   - **src/links/edit.js**: `check`, `parseCode`, `parseNumber`, `countOf` (BigInt), `parseIndex(text,n)`, `parseLinks`, `parseMath`, `functionOf`, `signatureOf`, `theoryNotation(links, notation)`, `numberNotation`, `decimalOf`, `linksText(links, sep)`, `addLink`, `removeLink(links,k)`, `setReference(links,i,end,ref)`.\n\n   **Created in this session:**\n   - **src/links/style.js**\n     - Field helpers from settings/fields. `STYLE_SECTIONS` ids: shape, ends, lines, background, caption, image, experimental.\n     - Fields:\n       - shape: angles (mirror/fixed), sourceAngle, targetAngle, lens, tension, bulge, gap, free, loop, spread, rotation, padding;\n       - ends: start/startSize/startAngle, end/endSize/endAngle, middle/middleSize (shown via `when`);\n       - lines: strokeWidth 2.4, dash, linecap round, linejoin round, opacity, glow, palette (site/neon/pastel/warm/cold/print/mono/custom), monoColor;\n       - background: background solid (or transparent/linear/radial), bgColor #070b14, bgColor2 #1e1b4b, bgAngle 135, card true, cardColor #0d1220, cardOpacity 0.8, borderStyle solid (or dashed/dotted/double/none), border 0.6, borderColor #2b3b57, radius 10, inset 3;\n       - caption: none (or theory/pairs/number/links/custom), captionText (type 'text', max 80), captionColor #7d8aa3, captionSize 6, captionFont mono (or sans/serif);\n       - image: width and height 1024 (64–4096), quality 0.92;\n       - experimental (with a lead text): solve false, solveRange 60, solveStep 15.\n     - Per-link list fields `colors` and `turns` (strings \"a,b\" and \"s t,s t\").\n     - Exports:\n       - `STYLE_FIELDS`, `STYLE_DEFAULTS`, `PALETTES`;\n       - `normalizeStyle(raw)` clamps ranges, validates hex/enums/booleans and normalizes lists;\n       - `styleToParams` (non-defaults only) and `styleFromParams`;\n       - `linkColors(style,n)`, `linkTurns(style,n)`, `withTurns(style, turns)`, `withColor(style,n,i,value)` (switches the palette to custom);\n       - `shapeOfStyle(style, n, extraTurns)`;\n       - `LOOKS` (card, black, transparent, paper, blueprint, neon, social 1200×630 with a theory caption) and `applyLook(style,id)`, which keeps turns, solve, solveRange and solveStep, and keeps the size unless the look sets one;\n       - `SIZES` (512², 1024², 2048², Instagram 1080², OG 1200×630, X 1600×900, Stories 1080×1920).\n   - **src/links/render.js**\n     - `escapeXml`, `captionOf(links, style, notation)`.\n     - `networkSvg(links, rawStyle, {notation, extraTurns, title})`:\n       - normalizes the style; the viewBox's shorter side is 100 units;\n       - `backdrop` writes defs for the linear/radial gradient, the card rect with fill-opacity, and the border (dashed/dotted dasharray, double draws a second rect at b*2.5);\n       - `edge = card ? inset : 0`, `room = captionSize*2.2`, `side = max(SIZE-room-2*edge,10)`, and the glyph is placed with `translate(x y) scale(side/SIZE)`;\n       - a glow filter (feGaussianBlur stdDeviation glow*0.5 + feMerge);\n       - dash arrays relative to the width (dots need non-butt caps);\n       - filled markers get `fill=color`;\n       - the caption text uses textLength fitting when the estimated width is too long;\n       - an `<title>` and aria-label \"Links network 01₃ 20₃\".\n   - **src/links/collisions.js**\n     - `pairCost(a,b,middles)`: crossings (weight 1) plus close points within NEAR=0.09 (0.25 each), excluding points within MIDDLE=0.14 of any middle. SAMPLES=16 per segment.\n     - `overlapCost(links, shape)` adds a turning penalty of 0.002 per degree.\n     - `solveCollisions(links, shape, {range=60, step=15, passes=3})` returns `{delta, turns, before, after}` (coordinate descent per end).\n   - **experiments/issue-17-collisions.mjs**: results were 22 13 31: 11.25→0.64; 23 31 12: 22.5→0.54; a 9-link cycle: 29.25→20.65 in 488 ms. For the 720 classes of n=3: 507 better, 213 same, 0 worse.\n   - **src/links/export.js**: `fileName(code, ext)` (\"links-network-01-20.png\"), `svgBlob`, `FORMATS` (png; jpeg with ext jpg; webp), `rasterize(svg,{width,height,type,quality,fill})` (Image → canvas → toBlob), `download(blob,name)`, `copyText`, `copyImage` (ClipboardItem), `canShare(files)`, `shareTargets(url,text)` (x, telegram, vk, facebook, linkedin, reddit, bluesky, mastodon, whatsapp, email).\n   - **network/index.html**: copied from settings/index.html with a new description, og tags, canonical https://konard.github.io/network/, the title \"Links network editor — Konstantin Diachenko (konard)\", a short noscript, and the script /src/pages/network.jsx.\n   - **src/pages/network.jsx**: `mount(NetworkPage)`.\n   - **vite.config.js**: 'network' added to PAGES.\n   - **src/pages/NetworkEditor.jsx**\n     - `NotationField`: draft state `{text, at, error}`, where the draft is active only while `draft.at === value` (no effects); the error is shown with role alert.\n     - `Notations({links, notation, onLinks})` has the fields notation-theory (parseMath), notation-pairs, notation-number (parseNumber), notation-decimal (parseIndex) and notation-links (textarea, parseLinks), with an intro text that uses OF_LINKS / OF_NETWORKS genitives.\n     - `LinksTable({links, colors, turns, onLinks, onRemove, onColor, onTurn, onStep, onRandom})`: a table with source/target selects (0 — nothing, i — itself), a colour input, turn number inputs (-180..180 step 5), a remove button, and the actions Add a link, Previous/Next network, Random network, and Smallest renaming (disabled when n > 7; it uses `decode(canonical(links))`).\n     - Also exports `stepped(links, step)` (BigInt wrap) and `randomLinks(n, random)`.\n     - It uses the class `visually-hidden`.\n   - **src/pages/NetworkStyle.jsx**\n     - `readSaved()` / `writeSaved` with localStorage key 'network.styles', at most 12 styles.\n     - `Control` uses the same row classes as settings, with types range, toggle, color, text and select.\n     - `Looks({style,onStyle})`: look buttons, a size preset select, and save/apply/delete of saved styles.\n     - `StyleSections({style, onStyle, children, only})`: each section has a reset button, and `children` are rendered inside the experimental section.\n   - **src/pages/NetworkShare.jsx** (just written), `NetworkShare({code, links, svg, style, url, text})`:\n     - downloads of SVG, PNG, JPEG (with bgColor fill) and WebP, plus .lino;\n     - copy the link, the PNG image and the SVG code;\n     - Share… through navigator.share with the PNG file when possible;\n     - a URL input, social share links (`data-share`), a note that og:image is static, and a role=status message.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Plain node failed with ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND on extensionless imports; experiments now run with `npx vite-node`.\n   - render.js first version had a bug: defs were emitted before backdrop pushed the gradient defs, and the y computation was junk. Fixed by computing `back = backdrop(...)` first and using edge/room/side.\n   - In collisions.js I removed an unused final reassignment of `lines` and made `lines` const.\n   - NetworkEditor:\n     - `canonical` returns a string; it is now decoded;\n     - `plural` had been given an array instead of `{en,ru}` forms; fixed with the OF_LINKS / OF_NETWORKS constants;\n     - removed a BigInt plural hack (Number(count) is exact for n ≤ 9).\n   - The Russian/English plurals in the edit.js error message were fixed earlier.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **URL design:** `/network/?code=0120&<non-default style params>`, with `#share` scrolling to the share section. The URL fully defines the picture.\n   - **Solver performance:** it is fine for automatic use with useMemo keyed on the shape params; 9 links take about 0.5 s.\n   - **Gallery card plan:** each li holds `a.symbols__card href=\"/network/?code=0120\"` (wrapping Glyph and span) and a sibling `a.symbols__share href=\"/network/?code=0120#share\"` with an aria-label and an SVG icon made only of circle/line elements (no text), shown on :hover / :focus-within. The li title stays.\n   - **NetworkExample** (src/components/MetaTheory.jsx) should get an \"Edit and share this network\" link.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The only user message: \"Issue to solve: https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/issues/17 Your prepared branch: issue-17-c029b2b48293 Your prepared working directory: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1792853904677 Your prepared Pull Request: https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/18 Do not stop until every requirement of the issue and all required sub-issues is fully implemented and verified in this single pull request, in the widest requested scope, with no requested work deferred; work that is truly blocked must be reported as blocked and left unfinished, never presented as done. Proceed.\"\n   - The system repeatedly asked me to say in a few words what I'm doing; these were not user requests.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - **Write src/pages/NetworkPage.jsx:**\n     - read the URL (default code '11 22 12'), keep `links` and `style` state, and sync with `history.replaceState` (code digits without spaces plus `styleToParams`);\n     - scroll to the