[2026-10-24T15:44:14.709Z] [INFO]         "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Read, ToolSearch, Write, mcp__playwright__browser_navigate, mcp__playwright__browser_resize, mcp__playwright__browser_run_code_unsafe, mcp__playwright__browser_take_screenshot</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\nStatus for the user: the network editor page is built, all tests and checks pass, and the commits are pushed. I'm now taking browser screenshots for the case study and the PR.\n\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Solve https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/issues/17, \"Add a share option for all links variants\". The issue has no comments.\n   - Work in /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1792853904677 on branch `issue-17-c029b2b48293`, push only to that branch, and update the existing draft PR #18 (https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/18), keeping \"Fixes #17\" in its body.\n   - Do not stop until every requirement is implemented and verified.\n   - What the issue asks for:\n     - Each gallery card gets a share icon that shows only on mouse hover and leads to a separate editor/share page. Clicking the card itself also opens that page.\n     - The page has three editable representations of the network: the math notation of the theory, an N-ary number, and links notation.\n     - As many options as possible: angles, start/end shapes, colours, background (including transparent), card borders and their style.\n     - A choice between a card and a plain black background.\n     - Downloads of PNG and other formats, and sharing to social media.\n     - An experimental option that reduces line collisions.\n   - Finishing steps:\n     - `npm run check`, `npm run test:ci`, and passing CI;\n     - a case study at docs/case-studies/issue-17/README.md and a README \"Case studies\" entry;\n     - screenshots linked as `https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-17-c029b2b48293/<path>?raw=true`;\n     - remove `.gitkeep` (it still exists at the repo root);\n     - commit messages that are long, descriptive and end with \"(issue #17)\";\n     - merge main if needed and check comments on the issue and PR;\n     - `gh pr edit` for the title and description, then `gh pr ready 18`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Stack:** React 19 + Vite multi-page app (PAGES in vite.config.js, `network/index.html`, `src/pages/network.jsx` with `mount`). Vitest uses jsdom and @testing-library.\n   - **Tooling:** Prettier (singleQuote, printWidth 120). ESLint uses react-hooks v7. A husky/lint-staged pre-commit hook runs eslint --fix and prettier.\n   - **i18n and notation:** `useLang().t({en,ru})`, `plural(count, lang, forms)`, and `useNotation().notation` ('L' or 'R').\n   - **Network codes:** \"01 20\" means link i+1 is [source, target] in base n+1.\n   - **Gallery test constraints:**\n     - li textContent is only the math notation, so the share icon has no text;\n     - the 162 paths for n=2 still hold, because the icon is drawn with circles and lines only;\n     - the li title is kept.\n   - **URL:** `/network/?code=0120&<non-default style params>`, plus `#share` to jump to the share section.\n   - **Duplicate ids:** control ids are `style-<key>`, so the style sections now use `style-section-<id>` to avoid a clash.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   **Committed and pushed in 5 commits** (ff5f03c, be72b49, 7be35e9, af98b80, 2fea4b5 on top of b400fb6):\n   - **src/links/glyph.js:** the shape options, up to 9 links, and `glyphParts`.\n   - **src/settings/fields.js** and **src/pages/SettingsPage.jsx:** `formatValue` moved to fields.js.\n   - **src/links/edit.js, style.js, render.js, collisions.js, export.js**, the new **src/links/network.test.js** (15 tests), and **experiments/issue-17-collisions.mjs**.\n   - **style.js `normalizeList`** now trims trailing zero turns:\n     ```js\n     while (turns.length && turns[turns.length - 1].every((a) => a === 0)) turns.pop();\n     return turns.map((pair) => `${pair[0]} ${pair[1] ?? 0}`).join(',');\n     ```\n   - **src/pages/NetworkPage.jsx:**\n     - exports `DEFAULT_CODE='11 22 12'`, `readNetwork(search)` and `networkQuery(links, style)`, whose result is `?code=0120&...`;\n     - the default component keeps `links` and `style` state, calls `history.replaceState` in an effect, and scrolls to the hash on mount;\n     - the `solved` useMemo (solveCollisions) is keyed on `shapeKey` and `style.solve`;\n     - the `svg` useMemo calls networkSvg with `extraTurns: solved?.delta`;\n     - remove(k) also drops the turns and custom colours of link k;\n     - the preview div `.network__preview` (with `is-transparent`) has no role, because the SVG names itself;\n     - sections: notations, links and share as panels, and style with Looks plus StyleSections, whose experimental children are \"Write the turns into the table of links\" and \"Clear all turns\".\n   - **src/pages/NetworkEditor.jsx, NetworkStyle.jsx, NetworkShare.jsx:** NetworkStyle's section ids changed to `style-section-${section.id}`.\n   - **src/pages/network.css (new):**\n     - `.visually-hidden`;\n     - the network__layout grid (5fr/7fr) with a sticky `.network__view` (top 7.5rem);\n     - checkerboard for the transparent preview;\n     - panels, notations, links-table, looks, `.network__styles` grid, share;\n     - a media query at 900px.\n   - **src/pages/network.test.jsx (new, 12 tests):**\n     - gallery hrefs and the share icon;\n     - the NetworkExample link;\n     - readNetwork and networkQuery;\n     - stepped and randomLinks;\n     - the page renders every notation, with a unique-ids check;\n     - notation edit sync and the URL;\n     - invalid text gets an alert;\n     - the links table (reference, add, colour, turn, remove, next);\n     - card vs. plain black, \"End of a link\" and the Background combobox;\n     - the experimental solver;\n     - share buttons and links;\n     - saved styles.\n   - **network/index.html** and **src/pages/network.jsx**; vite.config.js has 'network' in PAGES.\n   - **src/components/NetworkGallery.jsx:**\n     - exports `networkHref(code)`, which returns `/network/?code=${code.replace(/ /g,'')}`;\n     - a `ShareIcon` made of circles and lines;\n     - each li holds `a.symbols__card` (Glyph plus span) and `a.symbols__share`, with href `...#share`, aria-label \"Share <math>\" and a title.\n   - **src/pages/pages.css:**\n     - `.symbols__grid li` is position: relative;\n     - `.symbols__card`;\n     - `.symbols__share` is absolute and opacity 0, shown on li:hover and :focus-visible;\n     - there is no touch-only rule, because the issue says the icon shows only on hover.\n   - **src/components/MetaTheory.jsx:** NetworkExample has the link `a.theory__edit` \"Edit and share this network\" to `networkHref(code)`.\n   - **src/links/links.test.js:** the test changed to \"1–9 links fit into a symbol\", with 10 links throwing.\n\n   **Local only, not committed:**\n   - ci-logs/ and .playwright-mcp/ were added to .git/info/exclude.\n   - Screenshot saved: docs/case-studies/issue-17/screenshots/network-desktop.png. It shows the 1440×1000 page for `?code=221331`: the heading \"Links network 22₄ 13₄ 31₄\", the card preview with 3 coloured links, and the Notations panel. The page looked correct in the light theme.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Preview role:** the preview div with role img contained an SVG that also has role img, so tests found multiple elements. I removed role and aria-label from the div.\n   - **Duplicate id `style-background`:** the section and the control had the same id. The sections now use `style-section-*`.\n   - **Test expectations:**\n     - strokeWidth max is 10, not 8;\n     - the glyph path combines line and markers, so the test now compares the first `M` segment;\n     - the label is \"End of a link\";\n     - Background is queried by combobox role;\n     - turns are trimmed, so the expected value changed.\n   - **links.test.js:** the old \"1–4 links\" test failed as expected after the change; it was updated.\n   - **Checks:** the final `npm run check` passed. Its only warning is pre-existing: experiments/collect-registries.cjs has 1354 lines. vitest: 27 files and 560 tests passed. `npm run build` succeeded (build/network/index.html).\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Everything is implemented, tested and pushed.\n   - The vite preview server is running in the background on port 4317 (log in ci-logs/preview.log), and Playwright is open at http://localhost:4317/network/?code=221331 with a 1440×1000 viewport.\n   - The console shows only WebGL GPU-stall warnings and no errors.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"Issue to solve: https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/issues/17 Your prepared branch: issue-17-c029b2b48293 Your prepared working directory: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1792853904677 Your prepared Pull Request: https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/18 Do not stop until every requirement of the issue and all required sub-issues is fully implemented and verified in this single pull request, in the widest requested scope, with no requested work deferred; work that is truly blocked must be reported as blocked and left unfinished, never presented as done. Proceed.\"\n   - The system repeatedly asked me to say in a few words what I'm doing. These were not new requests.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - **More screenshots** in docs/case-studies/issue-17/screenshots/:\n     - full page;\n     - the style section;\n     - the share section;\n     - the plain black look;\n     - the transparent look;\n     - collision reduction before and after (e.g. code 221331);\n     - gallery hover share icon on /art/#symbols (hover `.symbols__grid li`);\n     - a mobile view (e.g. 390×844);\n     - dark theme, if possible.\n   - Check that the layout has no visual problems.\n   - Write docs/case-studies/issue-17/README.md covering:\n     - the requirements mapped to implementation and tests;\n     - design decisions (URL keeps everything; do we need a card? both, as looks);\n     - collision solver results (n=3: 507 better, 213 same, 0 worse; 22 13 31: 11.25→0.64; 9-link cycle 29.25→20.65 in 488 ms);\n     - limits (og:image is static on GitHub Pages; social share links share the URL, and images are attached via download, copy or the Web Share API);\n     - screenshots.\n   - Add a README \"Case studies\" entry and mention /network/.\n   - Remove `.gitkeep`, then commit (ending \"(issue #17)\") and push.\n   - Check CI (`gh run list --repo konard/konard.github.io --branch issue-17-c029b2b48293`), merge origin/main if needed, and check issue and PR comments.\n   - `gh pr edit 18` with a title and description: Fixes #17, summary, screenshots using `?raw=true` links, how to test, and test notes. Then `gh pr ready 18`.\n   - Stop the preview server and close the browser at the end.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just taken the first Playwright screenshot (docs/case-studies/issue-17/screenshots/network-desktop.png) of `http://localhost:4317/network/?code=221331` and viewed it. The page renders correctly: heading, preview card with the 3 links, and the editable notation fields.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   - Take the remaining screenshots with Playwright:\n     - a full-page shot of /network/?code=221331;\n     - the \"Plain black\" look and the transparent look;\n     - the experimental \"Reduce overlaps automatically\" before and after;\n     - the share section (`#share`);\n     - a mobile viewport;\n     - /art/#symbols with a hovered card that shows the share icon.\n   - Then write the case study README and the README entry, remove .gitkeep, commit and push, and update PR #18 with `gh pr edit` and `gh pr ready 18` after CI passes.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/box/.claude/projects/-tmp-gh-issue-solver-1792853904677/4b241afc-c5bf-4ea5-a425-f0bcdd392493.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."
